## 1. Starting endpoint

At the beginning of the run C-I was already closed.  The live gate was C-II: exclude
every sufficiently large triangle-free global source selected first to minimize unit
contacts and then diameter pairs, retaining all contact-isolated source points.

The first requested whole-source endpoint was

\[
\delta_K+\mathscr O_A\ge c_0P_K.
\tag{1.1}
\]

A useful algebraic observation made at the start of the run is that (1.1) is exactly

\[
D^2\ge\frac{2\sqrt3}{\pi}(n-1).
\tag{1.2}
\]

Indeed

\[
\delta_K+\mathscr O_A-c_0P_K
=
\frac{\pi D^2}{4}-a_0(n-1),
\]

because the source-hull area cancels.  The canonical strict translated-lattice
comparison gives the strict reverse inequality.  Consequently any proof of (1.1) must
use information absent from generic force-hull near-circularity; improving force-hull
area alone cannot reach it.

The alternate post-ZF exact endpoint was

\[
b+Q>2h,
\]

while ZF gives the opposite stress-rank requirement.  The run therefore attacked the
exact post-ZF defect ledgers rather than trying to derive (1.1) from near-radiality.

The new implication chain that emerged is

```text
exact PC/JC/ZK algebra
  -> all-phase renormalized currency mu
  -> FSDB/RSR + GU/JC/ZG + DD
  -> mu > 0.5947
  -> exact Eppstein component isoperimetry
  -> low mu forces overwhelmingly inactive source population
  + near-maximal full-source perimeter
  -> low mu forces a macroscopic inactive outer shell
  -> exact phase threshold u_pi.
```

