## 8. Regression tests and adversarial audit

| Regression / failure mode | Passed? | Exact reason |
| --- | --- | --- |
| regular odd shell | yes | GR/PT never infer near-perfect diameter matching or small response trace; shell lacks the source conclusions required to close PT-L |
| dense isolated filling | yes | EA's source-fraction conclusion uses `D=D(n)` through the global density asymptotic; arbitrary dense fillings lack that certificate |
| folded unit-contact path | yes | no Euclidean lower bound is inferred from contact-graph diameter; large `delta_r` is allowed |
| near-rhombic / square-grid component | yes | large internal face/boundary currency is allowed and is exactly the unresolved PT-H obstruction |
| singleton unloaded components | yes | separated explicitly in EA and contribute only `O(D)` because `c_I=O(D)` |
| bridges/repeated outer incidences | yes | Eppstein `k_r` is counted with multiplicity; Euler identity (3.2) remains valid |
| positive `s_Z` | yes | no step sets `s_Z=0`; equations (2.7)--(2.11) retain it exactly |
| contact-isolated source points | yes | never deleted; C65 identifies them and EA/PT count them in `n-v` |
| hull saturation | yes | never imposed; `K` and `F` are those of the contact/diameter-minimal selected source |
| RSR equality body | yes | GR endpoint exclusion uses exact pocket remainder and DD, not equality uniqueness |
| exact certificate arithmetic | yes | both new scripts use rational arithmetic/integer square roots and were rerun independently |

No finite competitor was claimed in this run, so there are no unverified pairwise
separation or diameter checks hidden behind a construction.

The uniform finite thresholds in GR are obtained by contradiction/diagonal sequence:
if no absolute positive gap above `0.5947` existed, one could choose `D_j>=j` with
`mu_j<0.5947+1/j`, pass to compact normalized parameters, and contradict the exact
limit exclusion.  Thus the quantifier is uniform over all post-ZF survivors, not
source-dependent.

