## 9. Failed routes and no-go results

### 9.1 Force-hull near-circularity cannot prove the requested whole-source inequality

The target

\[
\delta_K+\mathscr O_A\ge c_0P_K
\]

cancels `area(K)` exactly and reduces to (1.2).  A theorem only about `F` or about
near-circular area therefore has no direct sign leverage on the endpoint.

### 9.2 Attachment incidence does not upper-bound the full component currency

C37--C40 control attachment incidences and harmonic component graph diameter, but one
giant unloaded component can attach to many/all loaded vertices while carrying large
internal face defect `Q_r`.  The exact identity

\[
\delta_r+r_r=(k_r+Q_r)/2
\]

shows why: attachment counts do not control `Q_r`.  Treating C40 as a bound on
`delta_r+r_r` would be false.

### 9.3 A folded/indented contact boundary defeats cell-perimeter counting

The outer-face walk incidence `k_r` of a penny-graph component can be large inside one
convex attachment cell without forcing comparable attachment-cell perimeter.  Positive
KKT equilibrium does not imply that every component outer-face vertex is itself an
attachment.  Hence there is no valid direct C43-to-`sum k_r` upper inequality from the
current hypotheses.

### 9.4 Extreme-stress zeros are not C63-releasable rows

C63 releases active rows outside the **maximal KKT support** `E_*`.  After contact and
diameter-pair minimization, every remaining active row belongs to some normalized KKT
stress.  A coefficient that vanishes in one extreme stress is therefore not a weak row
and cannot be released by C63.  Extra stress dimension `s_Z>0` is not automatically a
finite descent direction.

### 9.5 Common circumcenter does not kill Woodall's odd cycle by parity alone

FS makes each diameter pair nearly antipodal about a common source center, but the
available endpoint/midpoint error is large enough to accumulate around an
`Theta(D)`-length odd cycle.  The regular odd shell is the exact regression.  A parity
argument without a summable error estimate is invalid.

### 9.6 Mixed 3-connectivity degree counting is too weak

The generic connectivity/degree consequences give only bounds of the scale
`s_B<=2h`, far above the required PT-H threshold.  An upper theorem must use geometry
or face structure, not minimum degree alone.

### 9.7 Many rattlers alone do not contradict global packing density

A near-triangular configuration scaled by `1+epsilon_D`, with `epsilon_D->0`, can have
no exact unit contacts while approaching optimal density.  Splitting Oler over force
and rattler regions reproduces an internal boundary term of order `D`.  Therefore even
the `>80%` inactive conclusion cannot be closed by leading area density alone.

### 9.8 A macroscopic inactive protrusion alone does not reduce `D`

All actual diameter endpoints lie in the positive loaded set by C65.  An inactive
point protruding beyond `F` may still be strictly inside every diameter constraint.
Moving it inward does not relax the KKT obstruction carried by the positive core.  A
valid PT-L rearrangement must coordinate enough of the inactive population and/or the
core to obtain strict diameter reduction.

