## 10. Literature imported/audited

### Rogalski--Saint Raymond (1985)

The sharp symmetric area/perimeter/diameter inequality remains a valid imported input.
The source says the disk attains equality, but its concluding Problem 2 asks whether
equality forces the disk.  Therefore the uniqueness statement previously used in one
report is not supported by that citation.  GR does not use it.

### Eppstein (2018)

David Eppstein, *Edge Bounds and Degeneracy of Triangle-Free Penny Graphs and
Squaregraphs*, JGAA 22(3) (2018), 483--499, already stored under `papers/primary/`.
The run checked the repository extraction `extracted/text/463.txt`, in particular the
outer-face/Voronoi isoperimetric lemmas and the resulting triangle-free penny-graph
edge deficit.  EA uses the more exact finite content of those lemmas rather than
summing an opaque `O(1)` from Theorem 4.

A targeted literature search did not locate a later proof of Swanepoel's stronger
conjectural `2n-2sqrt(n)` triangle-free penny-graph edge bound.  It was therefore not
imported.

### Woodall thrackle classification

This entered canonical `main` during the run at `1adc420e...` and is treated as an
upstream theorem, not new work here.  It sharpens the PT-H topology into the cyclic
odd-unicyclic case (`d_H=0`) or caterpillar-forest case (`d_H>0`), but no valid upper
bound on the internal component-face currency was derived from it.

